  "static_assessment": [
    "Planning locations are untrusted source bookkeeping; actual Index selects a committed concrete impl before effective equations. Values cannot prove their own premises.",
    "All relevant definitions receive symbolic scalar/type/purity checks. No-impl symbolic cycles execute no fabricated Self VM inputs. Effective graphs reject active cycles; an override can break a template cycle.",
    "Overridden Self defaults have separate DefaultCheck jobs against completed effective values; only after every job succeeds are effective literals published to actual impl member ordinals.",
    "Actual source member owner comes from full original member positions, not Span. The fixture inserts ordinary methods between A/B and independently checks each host/trait result.",
    "Completion coordinates are private current-request trace. Actual output moves are mapped explicitly; generated/late/ambiguous/unknown impls cannot manufacture completion through literals, matching names or spans.",
    "Coverage resolves unique actual trait/alias and frozen import ModuleId targets. Meta candidates and conflicting same-alias targets remain unknown; OtherConsumer does not grant Closed or general trait permission.",
    "The planner opt-in byte ledger uses the current remaining quota and prepays syntax/text/identity allocations before cloning. Returned actual Plan capacities remain charged; dropped scratch is refunded. Node/work ledgers are transferred without renewal. Ordinary Expand retains temporary=None accounting.",
    "Standalone Expand remains a definition/consumption boundary, not a full Source DefaultCheck executor. It explicitly rejects pending effective equations; no serialized witness/completion permission was added."
  ],
